  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I reviewed all 7 patients on \"DOAC dose review - week of 10/19/2026\" under RBC-PHARM-07. Four DOAC doses changed and three are correct as they were. Every change has a progress note giving the values used, the rule result and the cited records.\n\n**Doses changed**\n- **pt-0061 Irene Castellano:** apixaban 2.5 → 5 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). She is 74, 78 kg, SCr 1.02, so she meets none of the dose criteria. She was on 2.5 mg only because of itraconazole, and the 9/10 infectious disease letter says that course ended 8/14.\n- **pt-0041 Raymond Duquette:** apixaban 5 → 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0005). He meets no dose criteria, but he has an active itraconazole order (mr-00359) for toenail fungus. Itraconazole was left alone as the policy requires.\n- **pt-0038 Eugene Moravec:** rivaroxaban 15 → 20 mg daily (mr-t0007). CrCl is 56.1 using his actual weight of 96 kg and SCr 1.45. The May reduction was based on ideal body weight, which the policy does not allow.\n- **pt-0043 Marjorie Pellegrino:** rivaroxaban 20 → 15 mg daily (mr-t0011). A new creatinine of 1.25 (drawn 10/22, resulted during the review) gives a CrCl of 43.6.\n\n**No net change**\n- **pt-0003 Frank Delgado:** stays on rivaroxaban 20 mg daily (now mr-t0009). I first reduced it to 15 mg because St. Brigid reported creatinine 160 µmol/L. They then corrected it to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL) after an analyzer fault, which gives a CrCl of 59.9, so I put him back on 20 mg. A correction note is on file.\n- **pt-0002 Harold Vance:** stays on apixaban 2.5 mg twice daily (now mr-t0021). He now meets only the age criterion (82; weight 64.9 kg and SCr 1.21 have recovered), so I first increased him to 5 mg. A St. Brigid dermatology letter then arrived: he started itraconazole on 10/22 for 12 weeks, so I put him back on 2.5 mg. A correction note is on file. Re-review when the course ends, around mid-January 2027.\n\n**Left unchanged**\n- **pt-0062 Norman Fairweather:** apixaban 5 mg twice daily is correct. His ED creatinine was 150 µmol/L on 10/21, but the latest is 100 µmol/L (1.13 mg/dL) on 10/22, so only the age criterion (82) is met. I wrote a short note.\n\n**Arrivals during the review**\n- I completed all five new inbox items (inbox-a0001 to a0005) with comments.\n- Mr. Moravec sent a portal message with a home-scale weight of 185 lb. A self-reported weight doesn't count under the policy, so his 20 mg dose stands. My addendum note recommends a clinic weight at his next visit, but I didn't reply to him or create a task.\n- Mr. Duquette will also need re-review when his itraconazole course ends.\n- The older inbox items that were there before I started are untouched.",
